#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:5
#: c6da2f223ede4f3593592b2ef08c59e9
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:10
#: dc8472a5d51d4901b6d1fa461425f1da
msgid "The `Vac-U-Tug <http://www.vac-u-boat.com/Vacutug.htm>`__ is an ideal candidate for a first ArduRover Boat project. It's roomy, has comprehensive  build instructions targeted for inexperienced builders, and does not usually require extensive waterproofing of the ArduPilot electronic components. It's definitely not a speed boat, but is a great long duration lake/pond cruiser."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:13
#: e679c367b6a1469f8fe59478f1033f91
msgid "Parts List"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:15
#: 3d69650f4395454a856a15cc9cd1f48b
msgid "The kit includes the drive train and requires the addition of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:17
#: 0db07d10b9e24c668cb8f810fe64777c
msgid "A standard size servo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:18
#: 98aa72718a164f1aba59058207d4b9d5
msgid "A Brushed ESC with reverse (\"1060\" style), such as `this <https://www.ebay.com/sch/i.html?_from=R40&_trksid=m570.l1313&_nkw=1060+brushed+esc&_sacat=0>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:22
#: 377fc75f6ffa468a97b5b7b5ea5a97f5
msgid ":ref:`Autopilot Controller<common-autopilots>`. An Omnibus F4 Pro was used in this build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:23
#: 8b2e9cd32fec4985b90d731e26045ff3
msgid "GPS: Any UBLOX MN-8 class GPS with compass. BN-880 is an example, and was used in this build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:24
#: 7c7bbf7ccd384180a111a2473d614ea3
msgid "Receiver: Any 3 Channel, or more, TX/RX system. More channels allow more auxiliary functions to be implemented, like automatic waypoint learning, etc. Standard aircraft radios work well also."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:25
#: 89c432ca72354ccbb3dc8574a4655e86
msgid "Telemetry (optional but recommended): 3DR or other telemetry radio system, or via the receiver if it has that capability, like Dragonlink (bi-directional) or FRSky (downlink only). Directing the boat from a cell phone running a ground control station is great fun."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:26
#: b71cfe3a9fba4bd9938ad66b2758574e
msgid "Battery: A 6 cell NiMH 2000mah battery will give 1-2 hours of operation with a 2-3 km/hr top speed. A 3S 3000mah LIPO battery will provide extra speed and power (perhaps for rescuing disabled boats and pushing them to shore)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:27
#: e6e2b9ee267946ad84cd85adcd28746f
msgid "FPV Equipment (optional): A miniature video camera and video transmitter. A 5.8GHz 200mw transmitter will provide more than enough range in most situations. See :ref:`common-fpv-first-person-view` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:30
#: 364f8e7db78344cca06e363ff1583290
msgid "Build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:32
#: 51d65104673741af8a8064bef9ca625d
msgid "The build followed the manufacturer's instructions exactly, with a few minor deviations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:34
#: 6eca7f7ac98c4398a387ed1911dfd41f
msgid "Install the telemetry radio in the upper deck before gluing to lower deck"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:36
#: ea16372cbdae48e5a9144e1446acfa1b
msgid "Waterproof the GPS, since it is located in the most likely place to get wet if a wave broadsided the vessel. I 3D printed a small plastic case and sealed the GPS inside, assuring a waterproof seal around it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:38
#: a525a2711fb54ac5ab7a7a97a246cbe0
msgid "During ballasting step, in order to avoid rolling over while filling ballast cups on top deck, split the operation into two or more steps: putting the partial ballast in the plastic bags that will be used to mix them with epoxy in a later step, and placing them inside the hull below the cups before continuing to fill them with the final amounts of ballast. Keeping the center of gravity low."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:41
#: cacfaf5953024b41946f84aa6035a58e
msgid "Additional Build Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:43
#: 58e0c50d6c4f429ba0ea5610bb404a79
msgid "Mount the autopilot controller as shown below on the electronics deck."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:45
#: 6e49d3a7c4ff4146889d55f14d957d8d
msgid "Install the camera and video transmitter as shown below. Paint and glue the pilot house roof before  installing the video transmitter's antenna. After confirming that the camera is oriented and functioning correctly. Waterproof around its exit hole from the pilot house. Hot glue works well and can be removed in the future, if needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:47
#: aa41ba4c4127461d9b4e768b1172d043
msgid "Locate the components as shown below. Separating the GPS, video transmitter, and telemetry transmitter will prevent any interference between these systems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:59
#: abc1b24762ee476582d278d4d0d6e790
msgid "Setup Steps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:61
#: 04a79734399d4ce9bcbd26121843c5c9
msgid "Install the firmware"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:62
#: f59e74fa56e84e4faa2b6c6269d0661a
msgid "Set :ref:`FRAME_TYPE<FRAME_TYPE>` = 2 for boat."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:63
#: 17d594ee13d54a648fc28637542ad7e4
msgid "Connect steering servo to PWM output 1 and ESC to output 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:64
#: 8787a0b80a904568b79f0c13194f0896
msgid "Set :ref:`AHRS_ORIENTATIONM<AHRS_ORIENTATION>` orientation (in this build it's 6 for USB connector facing forward)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:65
#: a1faea08847d482db217aafaa4cf719a
msgid "Do Accelerometer, Compass, and RC calibrations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:66
#: 62e9849199e44b53be4d0123f89510f1
msgid "Set control modes. In this build, Manual, HOLD, Loiter, Steering, Acro,and Auto were used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:67
#: 30dfbd498d054f5aa272022f6cfa0442
msgid "Set up throttle failsafe and low battery failsafe, if desired. Set desired failsafe action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:68
#: 4d4dae619ae24ad7823cf16bcc629d23
msgid "Set up an auxiliary switch for Throttle Learn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:69
#: f2575879036740cb8f7815bffb90cfd3
msgid "Set :ref:`GCS_PID_MASK<GCS_PID_MASK>` = 1. For steering controller tuning in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:70
#: 7b69de3a3d704aeb9f09961064574783
msgid "On the bench, be sure that all modes function correctly, the steering servo moves in the correct direction in ACRO mode as you change the boat's heading, as well as under RC control in MANUAL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:73
#: 7b806c6b83814216865b0d8c1f18b045
msgid "First Float"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:74
#: 7ddd9513a16f4df9b23d231f609191a8
msgid "Verify properly operation sailing in MANUAL mode. Trim steering from TX to cruise straight. Then in the ground control station (GCS), set the steering servo's :ref:`SERVO1_TRIM<SERVO1_TRIM>` to the SERVO1's output value at neutral TX stick. Then set the :ref:`RC1_TRIM<RC1_TRIM>` (Assuming no RC remapping has been done) to the value of the channel at neutral stick, then return the trim to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:75
#: 69c41d6f9e4e4cb9ac449c13ff913b0a
msgid "Next sail in ACRO. At low speed, determine the turn rate, ie how many secs for a complete turn divided by 360 and enter this in the :ref:`ACRO_TURN_RATE<ACRO_TURN_RATE>` parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:76
#: 28659c02fc2b41e3a8c247bc4a7fad25
msgid "Next do the :ref:`rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed` and  :ref:`rover-tuning-steering-rate`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/reference-frames-vacutug.rst:78
#: 5449176a479746d498cba999ccf66f9a
msgid "At this point, it will be tuned well enough with the defaults in the navigation controller to navigate and return to home. Further :ref:`rover-tuning-navigation` can be done, if desired."
msgstr ""
